WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.100
Lycopene is the
phytonutrient

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.500
that gives tomatoes
their bright red color.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.520
It’s among the most potent
of carotenoid antioxidants,

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.220
so what happened
when researchers

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.380
pitted lycopene and
whole tomatoes

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.240
against prostate cancer?

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.680
Check it out.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.734
"Lycopene Supplements vs. Prostate Cancer &amp;
Tomato Sauce vs. Prostate Cancer"

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:28.020
Back in the '80s, the Adventist Health Study
found strong protective relationships

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.780
against prostate cancer with
increasing consumption

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:35.220
of legumes, citrus, dried
fruit, nuts, and tomatoes.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:39.180
In the '90s, a Harvard study
focused attention on tomatoes,

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.460
which appeared to be
especially beneficial.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.480
They suspected it might be the red
pigment in tomatoes called lycopene,

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.660
which has greater antioxidant power
than some of the other pigments,

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:52.260
like the orange beta-carotene
pigment in carrots and cantaloupes.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.240
And lycopene dramatically kills off
prostate cancer cells in a petri dish,

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.640
even way down at the
levels one would expect

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.700
in one's blood stream after
just eating some tomatoes.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.820
So of course the Heinz
ketchup company,

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.340
along with manufacturers
of lycopene supplements,

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:12.300
petitioned the FDA to allow them to
print health claims on their products.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:17.100
They were essentially denied, saying
that the evidence was very limited

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:21.540
and preliminary, with no endorsement
allowed for ketchup or supplements.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:27.180
By that time, further population studies
had cast doubt on the lycopene theory.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.880
Consumers of high dietary
intakes of lycopene

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.520
didn't seem to have lower
cancer rates after all.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:36.120
But who has high dietary
intakes of lycopene?

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.120
Those that eat the most pizza;

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.900
so maybe it's no surprise
there are mixed results.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.980
What we need is to put
lycopene to the test.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.520
It started with a case study.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:54.540
A 62-year old man with terminal
prostate cancer, failed surgery,

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:58.560
failed chemotherapy, metastases
all over, spread to the bone.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.460
And so he was sent
to hospice to die.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:09.000
So he took it upon himself to initiate
phytotherapy, plant-based therapy,

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.780
taking the amount of lycopene found
in a quarter cup of tomato sauce

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.780
or a tablespoon of
tomato paste every day.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:21.780
His PSA, a measure of tumor
bulk, started out as 365,

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:26.760
but dropped to 140 the next
month, and then down to 8.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:31.680
His metastases started disappearing,
and as of his last follow-up

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.620
appeared to be living
happily ever after.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:39.960
But when given in higher dose pill
form, lycopene didn't seem to work.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:43.440
A 2013 review of all such
lycopene supplement trials

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:46.380
failed to support
the initial optimism.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:49.020
In fact, they were just happy
that the lycopene pills

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.500
didn't end up causing more cancer,
like beta-carotene pills did.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.200
But then came 2014.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.280
Researchers in Italy had been giving
the largest doses they could

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:02.580
of lycopene, selenium, and
isolated green tea compounds

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:05.040
to men with precancerous
prostate lesions,

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.740
hoping they could prevent
full-blown cancer.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:12.300
But in 2014, the expanded results
of a similar trial were published

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.660
in which selenium and vitamin E
supplements resulted in more cancer.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:16.740
Yikes!

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.020
So these researchers
stopped their trial

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:21.360
and broke the code to
un-blind the results.

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:25.200
And indeed, those taking high doses
of lycopene, green tea catechins,

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:30.000
and selenium appeared to get more cancer
than those who just got sugar pills.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:34.980
"The potential implications are dramatic,"
said the lead researcher,

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:38.220
"given the current massive
worldwide use of such compounds

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:42.180
as alleged preventive supplementations
in prostate and other cancers."

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.820
What went wrong?

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.780
Well, after the beta-
carotene pill debacle,

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:51.720
researchers measured
cellular damage at different

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.240
natural and unnatural
doses of beta-carotene.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:59.280
At dietary doses, beta-carotene
suppressed cellular damage,

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.440
but at higher supplemental doses,

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.640
it not only appeared to stop
working, but caused more damage.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.100
And the same with lycopene.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:11.040
Both lycopene and beta-
carotene afforded protection

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.860
against DNA damage at the
kinds of levels one might see

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:16.620
in people eating lots of
tomatoes or sweet potatoes,

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:20.340
levels comparable with those
seen in the blood of individuals

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.980
who consume a carotenoid-
rich healthy diet.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:26.400
However, at the kind of blood
concentrations that one might get

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.000
taking pills, the ability
to protect the cell against

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.400
such free radical damage
was rapidly lost.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.460
And indeed, the presence of high
levels of beta-carotene and lycopene

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.880
may actually serve to increase
the extent of DNA damage.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.260
So no wonder high dose
lycopene pills didn't work.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:48.180
Phytochemicals may be
guardians of our health,

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.140
but the safety of consuming
concentrated extracts is unknown.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.140
The protective benefits of
a phytochemical-rich diet

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:58.980
are best obtained by
whole plant foods.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:02.640
The food industry has
different ideas, though.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:08.580
Soon there may be phytochemical-
fortified bacon, martinis, and ice cream,

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:11.100
says this article in the
Journal of Food Technology.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:15.480
If they can find just the right
mix of plant compounds,

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:19.860
they hope to reconstruct foods that
once contributed to illness and disease

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.995
to offer significant
health benefits.

00:05:26.338 --> 00:05:28.680
"Occasionally...positive
things happen in the field

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:32.100
of cancer prevention science
to popular, good-tasting foods."

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.520
Yes, broccoli family
vegetables are wonderful,

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.280
but may be a hard food
for the public to swallow.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:41.940
By contrast, who doesn't
like tomatoes?

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:45.120
But studies using high dose
supplements of lycopene,

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.640
the antioxidant red pigment
in tomatoes thought to be

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:48.960
the active anti-cancer ingredient,

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:52.920
failed over and over again
to prevent or treat cancer,

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.800
and may even end
up promoting it,

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.680
since at the high levels one
can get with supplements,

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.560
lycopene may actually
act as a pro-oxidant.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.140
But lycopene
doesn't appear

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:06.660
to be effective at
lower doses either.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:08.460
There is a strong
protective correlation

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:11.400
between the intake of actual
whole fruit and vegetables

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.380
and the incidence
of certain cancers,

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:16.500
but when we supplement
with only a single compound

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:19.380
isolated in pill form,
we may upset

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:22.560
the healthy natural
balance of antioxidants.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:26.760
It does seem to be
quite the human hubris

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:29.160
to think we can reproduce
the beneficial effects

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.900
of consuming entire
fruits and vegetables

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:33.600
by giving supplements
of a single phytochemical,

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.720
which would normally interact
with thousands of other compounds

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:39.600
in the natural matrix
Mother Nature intended.

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:42.780
In addition to lycopene,
other carotenoids in tomatoes

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:46.620
include beta-carotene,
gamma-carotene, zeta-carotene,

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:49.980
phytofluene, and phytoene,
all of which are known

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:52.560
to accumulate in
human prostate tissue.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:55.440
And there are also numerous
non-carotenoid compounds

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:57.840
in tomatoes that may
have anti-cancer activity,

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.320
not to mention all the compounds
we have yet to even characterize.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:04.920
But it's not about finding
the one magic bullet;

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:06.900
the anti-cancer effects
of carotenoids

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:10.860
and other phytonutrients may
reside in their combined activity.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.020
For example, at
low concentrations

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:16.140
of the tomato compounds
phytoene, phytofluene,

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:19.320
and lycopene found in most
people who eat normal amounts

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:21.180
of tomatoes, there's
very little effect

00:07:21.180 --> 00:07:24.000
on cancer cell growth
in vitro, used separately,

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.040
but combine them
all together

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.240
and a non-effective dose
plus a non-effective dose

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:34.080
becomes effective somehow,
significantly suppressing

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:35.700
prostate cancer cell growth.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:39.180
And the same synergy
can be seen across foods.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:42.720
Curcumin, the yellow pigment
in turmeric and curry powder,

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:46.200
tomato extracts, and the vitamin E
found in nuts and seeds

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.780
do little to inhibit
pro-growth signaling

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.580
of prostate cancer cells—
less than 10%.

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:55.140
But all three together suppresses
growth signaling like 70%.

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:58.500
The whole is greater
than the sum of its parts.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:02.940
So how about instead of giving
cancer patients lycopene pills,

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:06.000
we give them some
tomato sauce?

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.940
Thirty-two patients with
localized prostate cancer

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:12.600
were given three quarters of a cup
of canned tomato sauce every day

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:16.260
for three weeks before their
scheduled radical prostatectomy.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:20.760
In their bloodstream, PSA
levels dropped by 17.5%.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:23.640
PSA, prostate-specific antigen,

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:26.640
is a protein produced
by prostate gland cells,

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:29.160
and elevated blood levels
are routinely used

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:31.920
to monitor the success
of cancer treatment.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:35.820
It was surprising to find
that in just 3 weeks,

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:39.600
a tomato sauce-based dietary
intervention could decrease

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:42.660
PSA concentrations in
men with prostate cancer.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:46.320
Also, free radical
damage of the DNA

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:48.120
in their white blood
cells dropped by 21%.

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:53.040
Imagine how antioxidant poor their
diet must have been beforehand,

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:56.580
if less than a cup of tomato
sauce a day could reduce

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:58.980
DNA damage by
more than a fifth.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.420
OK, but what did they
find in their prostates?

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:06.960
Human prostate tissue is thought
to be particularly vulnerable

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.240
to oxidative DNA damage
by free radicals,

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:11.160
which are thought
to play a critical role

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:13.020
in all stages of
cancer formation.

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:15.360
This may be for a
number of reasons,

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:18.000
including fewer
DNA repair enzymes.

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:21.660
Well, the researchers had
tissue samples taken

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:25.183
before the tomato sauce from
biopsies, and tissue samples

00:09:25.183 --> 00:09:27.120
from the surgery after the
three weeks of tomato sauce,

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:32.100
and resected tissues from tomato
sauce-supplemented patients

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:36.420
had 28% less free radical
damage than expected.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:41.100
Here's the DNA damage in the
prostate before the tomato sauce,

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:45.540
and here's after,
just 20 days of sauce.

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:49.620
And what's interesting is
that there was no association

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:51.720
between the level of
lycopene in the prostate

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:53.040
and the protective effects.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.800
Tomatoes contain a
whole bunch of things,

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:59.400
some of which may be even
more powerful than lycopene.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:04.200
Regardless, in contrast to the
lycopene supplements alone,

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:07.080
the whole food intervention
seemed to help.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.260
To see if lycopene
plays any role at all,

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:12.960
one would have to test
a lycopene-free tomato—

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:16.320
in other words,
a yellow tomato.

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:21.060
So what if you compared red
tomatoes to yellow tomatoes,

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:23.400
which have all the non-lycopene
tomato compounds,

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.740
to straight lycopene in a pill.

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:29.580
So they fed people red tomato
paste, yellow tomato paste,

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:33.600
lycopene pills, or placebo pills,
and then dripped their blood

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:37.080
on prostate cancer cells
growing in a petri dish.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:40.680
Compared to those not eating
anything, the red tomato serum,

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.960
the blood from those
who ate red tomato paste

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:45.720
significantly decreased
the prostate cancer cell's

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:48.600
expression of a growth-promoting
gene called cyclin D1.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:52.080
This downregulation of the gene
by the red tomato consumption

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:54.720
may contribute to lower
prostate cancer risk

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:56.700
by limiting cell proliferation.

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:00.660
The red tomato seemed to
work better than the yellow,

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:05.580
so maybe the lycopene
helped, but not in pill form.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:10.620
This gene was not regulated
by the lycopene pill serum,

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:13.020
indicating that maybe
it's something else.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:16.440
And lycopene alone
significantly upregulated

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.600
procarcinogenic genes.

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:20.640
Therefore, it can be stated

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:23.940
that tomato consumption
may be preferable.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:26.580
So what's the best way?

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:30.660
A spouse wrote in to the editor
of the Harvard Men's Health Watch

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:34.560
saying his or her husband wants
to have pizza for his prostate,

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:38.760
to which the doctor replied, fine,
but how about cheese-free pizza

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:40.620
with broccoli instead
of pepperoni,

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:44.216
or he can just drink
some tomato juice.

